# Host architecture

**Moral:** This repo consumes providers. It does not fork them. Host logic is Go. AI exits only through Polypus.

Detail lives in [docs/ai-provider-seam.md](docs/ai-provider-seam.md), [docs/pimalaya-setup.md](docs/pimalaya-setup.md), and [docs/report-only-eval.md](docs/report-only-eval.md). Go quality: skill `golang-quality`. Operator workflow: skill `should-i-read-operator`. Operator home config: skill `operator-config` (`go tool task init` → `~/.config/should-i-read/config.yaml`).

## Provider boundaries

**CONSTRAINT:** Paths under `providers/` are nested repositories when present. Agents MUST treat them as read-only black boxes for product work.

- MUST: use provider CLIs, configs, and documented surfaces from the host when a provider is still in tree
- MUST: resolve ownership with `git -C <path> rev-parse --show-toplevel` before any write in that tree
- MUST NOT: edit, patch, or add features inside a provider to satisfy a host need
- MUST NOT: stage provider file bytes as ordinary host files
- NEVER: propose "just this once" changes inside a nested provider so classify/chat can hit Polypus

Enforcement: planned diff paths; `git -C providers/<name> status` stays clean for host tasks when that tree exists
Violation: STOP, move the work to host Go under this repo, re-verify

CORRECT:
```text
Host Go CLI syncs via Neverest/pimdir, writes a snapshot, then calls Polypus.
providers/ working trees unchanged.
```

PROHIBITED:
```text
Edit a nested provider's AI client to inject POLYPUS_BASE_URL for this host.
```

## Host language

**CONSTRAINT:** New host product and orchestration code MUST be Go.

- MUST: put host binaries, packages, and tests in this repository (for example `cmd/`, `internal/`)
- MUST: follow skill `golang-quality` when generating or completing Go
- MUST NOT: add host feature logic in TypeScript, Python, or shell beyond thin wrappers that invoke Go or documented Make targets
- MUST NOT: implement unwanted-mail / Jev / clustering logic inside a nested provider tree

Enforcement: new feature files are `.go` (or Go module scaffolding) under the host root
Violation: STOP, rewrite as Go on the host, delete the non-Go host feature path

CORRECT:
```text
cmd/unwanted-report/main.go talks to Polypus and writes tmp/unwanted-report-*.json
```

PROHIBITED:
```text
scripts/classify_with_jev.py as the product path for classification
```

## AI gateway

**CONSTRAINT:** All host AI HTTP MUST use Polypus only: resolve `polypus.base_url`, then `POLYPUS_BASE_URL`, then default `http://127.0.0.1:1320`.

- MUST: call OpenAI-compatible Polypus routes (`/v1/chat/completions`, `/v1/embeddings`, `/v1/models`, `/health`)
- MUST: fail closed when `./scripts/check-polypus.sh` fails before AI work
- MUST NOT: dial OpenRouter cloud, Ollama, Cloudflare, LM Studio, or TypeSafe/Jev from the host
- MUST NOT: enable embedded llama.cpp, OpenRouter, or Ollama for this host's AI features
- NEVER: store remote leaf-provider base URLs in host or nested-provider client config for this project

Enforcement: grep new code for `openrouter.ai`, `11434`, `typesafe.ai`, and non-loopback AI bases; require Polypus health before AI runs
Violation: STOP, route through Polypus (or document blocked until Polypus is up), re-verify

CORRECT:
```text
Go client: POST http://127.0.0.1:1320/v1/chat/completions with allow-listed model id
```

PROHIBITED:
```text
Set OPENROUTER_API_KEY so in-app classify "just works" against openrouter.ai
```

## Unwanted mail (Jev path)

**CONSTRAINT:** Until evaluation exit criteria in [docs/report-only-eval.md](docs/report-only-eval.md) pass, unwanted-mail automation MUST stay report-only.

- MUST: produce decisions, clusters, and TLDRs as host artifacts (for example under `tmp/`)
- MUST: keep Jev as typed decisions via Polypus; keep TLDR on a chat model via Polypus
- MUST NOT: delete, trash, spam-folder, or mark-read mail as part of the first milestone
- MUST NOT: call Jev/TypeSafe directly without Polypus

Enforcement: no mailbox-mutation calls in the report pipeline; mode flag `report_only`
Violation: STOP, remove mutation, keep report artifact only

CORRECT:
```text
Go report runner writes tmp/unwanted-report-<ts>.json; mailbox unchanged
```

PROHIBITED:
```text
Auto-move high-confidence spam to Trash from the first Jev integration
```

## Dos and don'ts (summary)

| Do | Don't |
|----|-------|
| Use host `configure` / `go tool task mail:readiness|mail:sync|mail:export` for mail | Patch nested providers for host needs |
| Write host orchestration in Go | Put product logic in provider trees |
| Send all AI through Polypus (`POLYPUS_BASE_URL` / config) | Point clients at leaf AI vendors |
| Keep unwanted-mail report-only until eval | Delete or quarantine mail early |

## Pre-change checklist

- [ ] **Provider untouched:** No planned writes under `providers/`
      Method: Review the change list
      Pass: Only host paths (and docs/rules in this repo)
      Fail: STOP, redesign as host Go + provider CLI use
- [ ] **Go host code:** New feature code is Go
      Method: File extensions and module layout
      Pass: `.go` under host `cmd/` / `internal/` (or agreed host layout)
      Fail: STOP, rewrite in Go
- [ ] **Polypus only:** AI base URL is Polypus
      Method: Grep for foreign AI bases and keys
      Pass: Only `POLYPUS_BASE_URL` / `127.0.0.1:1320`
      Fail: STOP, remove direct vendor dials
- [ ] **Report-only:** Unwanted-mail path does not mutate mail
      Method: Scan for trash/spam/delete/mark-read in the new path
      Pass: Artifact output only
      Fail: STOP, strip mutations
